node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.DS_Store
e2e/out
coverage
dist-single
dist-live

# Environment files. `.env.example` is the only one that belongs in the repository —
# everything else is somebody's real configuration, and a committed key is a leaked key
# even after the commit that removed it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dist-server

# Photographs. The folder's README is the only thing in it that belongs in the repository:
# every image is the owner's to license, and a committed photograph nobody holds the rights
# to is a legal problem that survives the commit that removed it — the same reasoning as the
# environment files above. `scripts/photo-placeholder.mjs` writes obviously-fake stand-ins
# here so the illustrated layout can be exercised locally; those must never be pushed either.
public/photos/*
!public/photos/README.md
